 "fingerprint": "19df30863d03a78fc5860912cdf0e0ed68bfe2da261dab207ca4dc272e77fe58",
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "<b>Chapter 3</b>",
   "bbox": [
    285,
    57,
    353,
    75
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "<b>Divisions of a sign</b>",
   "bbox": [
    257,
    85,
    381,
    103
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "1. The ten-fold division of the Zodiac is known as Dasa vargas (Vargas mean ",
   "bbox": [
    121,
    137,
    556,
    152
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "divisions). Under the scheme of Dasavarga the various divisions are as Under :—",
   "bbox": [
    85,
    161,
    541,
    176
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "(1) Rasi ",
   "bbox": [
    157,
    185,
    205,
    201
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Each Rasi 30° ",
   "bbox": [
    258,
    185,
    342,
    201
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "(2) Hora ",
   "bbox": [
    157,
    201,
    208,
    217
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "2 parts of a Rasi of 15° each. ",
   "bbox": [
    258,
    201,
    424,
    217
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "(3) Drekkana ",
   "bbox": [
    157,
    217,
    234,
    233
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "3 parts of a Rasi of 10° each. ",
   "bbox": [
    258,
    217,
    424,
    233
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "(4) Trimsamsa ",
   "bbox": [
    157,
    233,
    242,
    249
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "5 parts of 5°, 7° or 8° each. (All parts ",
   "bbox": [
    258,
    233,
    471,
    249
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "are not equal) ",
   "bbox": [
    258,
    249,
    339,
    265
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "(5) Saptamsa ",
   "bbox": [
    157,
    266,
    234,
    281
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "7 parts of 4°-17\"-8\" each. ",
   "bbox": [
    258,
    266,
    405,
    281
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "(6) Navamsa ",
   "bbox": [
    157,
    282,
    232,
    297
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "9 parts of 3°-20 each. ",
   "bbox": [
    258,
    282,
    382,
    297
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "(7) Dasmamsa ",
   "bbox": [
    157,
    298,
    241,
    313
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "10 parts of 3°each. ",
   "bbox": [
    258,
    298,
    367,
    313
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "(8) Dwadasamsa 12 parts of 2°-30' each. ",
   "bbox": [
    157,
    314,
    392,
    329
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "(9) Shodasamsa 16 parts of l°-16'-52\" each. ",
   "bbox": [
    157,
    330,
    413,
    345
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "(10) Shastyamsa 60 parts of 30' each. ",
   "bbox": [
    157,
    346,
    375,
    362
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Vargottama is the name given to that particular Navamsa in a Rasi which ",
   "bbox": [
    121,
    386,
    556,
    402
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "bears the same sign as that of Rasi itself.",
   "bbox": [
    85,
    410,
    313,
    426
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "2. If amongst the ten vargas only the Rasi, Hora, Drekkana, Navamsa, ",
   "bbox": [
    121,
    435,
    556,
    450
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Dwadasamsa and Trimsamsa are taken into consideration, the divisions are known ",
   "bbox": [
    85,
    459,
    556,
    474
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "as Shad vargas. If we add Saptamsa division to them, the 7 kinds of divisions are ",
   "bbox": [
    85,
    483,
    556,
    498
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "known as Sapta vargas.",
   "bbox": [
    85,
    507,
    216,
    523
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Some learneds have taken the view that the effect emanating from Navamsa ",
   "bbox": [
    121,
    531,
    556,
    547
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "is equal to that of Rasi and Bhava.",
   "bbox": [
    85,
    555,
    277,
    571
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "3. In Rasis the effect is full. In the Shodasamsa, Dasmamsa and Shastyamsa ",
   "bbox": [
    121,
    579,
    556,
    595
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "divisions (Vargas) it is one-fourth. In the other vargas it is half. In an odd Rasi, the ",
   "bbox": [
    85,
    604,
    556,
    619
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "planets are said to be in 'infancy, in boyhood, youth, in middle age and in very old ",
   "bbox": [
    85,
    628,
    556,
    643
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "age (near death), according to first, second, third, fourth and last six degree ",
   "bbox": [
    85,
    652,
    556,
    667
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "portions respectively reached by them in a sign. But in an even sign this is in the ",
   "bbox": [
    85,
    676,
    556,
    692
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "reverse order.",
   "bbox": [
    85,
    700,
    161,
    716
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Notes — In Aries, Gemini, Leo, Libra, Sagittarius and Aquarius there is ",
   "bbox": [
    121,
    724,
    556,
    740
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "infancy up to 6 degrees, up to 12° boyhood, from there to 18° it is youth and up to ",
   "bbox": [
    85,
    749,
    556,
    764
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "28",
   "bbox": [
    313,
    793,
    325,
    806
   ]
  }
 ]
}